+;; ── Admission<S> — the `-on-connect` return type (arc 278 connection-lifecycle-ops) ────────
+;;
+;; `Outcome`'s five variants cannot express a refusal (no client exists yet to reply Stop to,
+;; and every OTHER arm's exhaustive match over Outcome would have to grow an arm legal in
+;; exactly one place — an unreachable case that accumulates lies). `-on-connect` gets its own
+;; result type instead: keep the connection (state threads on) or refuse it (state threads on
+;; too — the id was still minted, STOP-8 — and a cause is told to the client on the way out).
+;;
+;; NAME — ratified 2026-08-10 off the design stone's candidate list (Admission · AdmitOutcome ·
+;; ConnectionOutcome · Gate); `Admission` reads as "was this connection admitted", the exact
+;; question `-on-connect` answers. `:wat::kernel::ConnectOutcome` (the CLIENT-side dial result:
+;; Connected/Refused/Rejected/Failed) is a DIFFERENT type answering a different question from the
+;; other end of the wire — this is the SERVER's admission decision, not the client's dial result.
+(:wat::core::defenum :wat::service::Admission<S> :wat::enum::Pure
+  :Accept [state <- :S]                                   ;; keep the connection; state threads on
+  :Refuse [state <- :S  cause <- :wat::kernel::Failure])   ;; tell the client, drop the peer, keep serving
